                         "id":  "meridian",
                         "name":  "Meridian",
                         "tagline":  "Triton\u0027s browser and web runtime, built on Chromium.",
                         "description":  "Meridian is Triton\u0027s Chromium-based browser and web runtime. Built on **JCEF** (Java Chromium Embedded Framework), it renders the modern web inside Echelon without depending on an outside browser.\n\nMeridian doesn\u0027t only show pages. Web interfaces and Progressive Web Apps run as first-class Echelon apps: a PWA or self-hosted web UI opens in its own Meridian window, sits on the desktop as a tile, and behaves like any other Triton program.\n\n## Selenium integration\n* **Scripting:** inject and run scripts against loaded pages to customize, extend, or connect web content to Triton.\n* **Automation:** drive pages programmatically for navigation, form filling, data extraction, and repeatable workflows.\n* **Web apps as Triton apps:** wrap web interfaces and PWAs so they launch, dock, and run inside Echelon.\n\nFormerly ChromeSD. Meridian is the bridge between Triton and the web.",
                         "version":  "1.1.3",
                         "author":  "ZeroC0deT1me",
